      "narration": "A fixed indemnity plan pays a stated dollar amount when a covered event occurs: 200 dollars per hospital day, 75 dollars per physician visit, 1,500 dollars per surgery. The payment is the same whether the bill is small or large, and it goes to the insured unless assigned. Because the benefit is not tied to the actual expense, fixed indemnity is an excepted benefit outside the Affordable Care Act rules, and federal and Maryland law require clear notice that it is not comprehensive coverage. It can soften deductibles or lost wages for Elena’s coworker; it cannot replace her medical plan.",
